### 8. PrivAudit: A Dual-Lens Auditing Framework for Website Privacy Practices under the CCPA
* **Speaker:** Mohammad Mustafa Daud
* **Slides:** [PrivAudit: A Dual-Lens Auditing Framework for Website Privacy Practices under the CCPA](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-maprg-privaudit-a-dual-lens-auditing-framework-for-website-privacy-practices-under-the-ccpa-01)
* Mohammad Mustafa Daud presented PrivAudit (CCS 2024), a framework combining LLM-based privacy policy analysis with browser-based script/cookie tracking analysis to audit compliance under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA).
* Key findings:
  * Script-based cookie attribution revealed that up to 40% of third-party trackers write cookies as first-party in the cookie jar.
  * Global Privacy Control (GPC, `Sec-GPC`) header handling: Enforcing GPC reduced third-party targeting cookies by 41% on CCPA-subject sites, but up to 40% of sites claiming to honor GPC showed zero reduction in targeting cookies when GPC was enabled.
  * 50% of sites stating they do not sell personal data still set third-party targeting cookies on the initial landing page.
* PrivAudit serves as an automated auditing tool for regulatory agencies (such as the CPPA) to detect disclosure-behavior discrepancies at scale.

